{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1481","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1481","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1481\",\"parent_revision\":\"53663133c2258b6e360bd8ff9d14b8c0023c079e3b41c6434cce825ff9d48af3\",\"root_revision\":\"53663133c2258b6e360bd8ff9d14b8c0023c079e3b41c6434cce825ff9d48af3\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`sam_status` returns task counts by status but no cycle time, throughput, or stuck-task detection. An agent cannot tell how long a task has been in-progress or whether it exceeded a reasonable duration.\\n\\n`dispatch_wave_status` provides per-wave detail but requires one call per wave with no aggregate endpoint \u2014 orchestrators must iterate waves and manually sum.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `Task.started`, `Task.completed`, `Task.last_activity` fields | AVAILABLE | `sam_schema/core/models.py:139\u2013147` |\\n| `PlanStatus.by_status` gives per-status counts | AVAILABLE | `sam_schema/core/models.py:500` |\\n| `DispatchSpawnSummary` cross-wave shape | AVAILABLE | `backlog_core/models.py:1403\u20131414` |\\n| `DispatchItemRecord.started_at`/`completed_at` per item | AVAILABLE | `backlog_core/models.py:1340\u20131358` |\\n| In-progress duration derivable from `now() - task.started` | DERIVABLE | Task model timestamps |\\n| Cross-wave aggregate derivable by iterating all waves for milestone | DERIVABLE | `mgr.get_all_waves()` or equivalent |\\n| `PlanStatus` has stuck_tasks, avg_cycle_time fields | MISSING | Confirmed absent in `models.py:492\u2013504` |\\n| Milestone-aggregate MCP tool | MISSING | No endpoint accepts milestone-only parameter |\\n| `stuck_threshold_minutes` parameter | MISSING | Not on any existing tool |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail \u2014 health metrics model fields exist in `Task`; they are not surfaced by any status tool  \\n**Aggregate endpoint**: new capability (shape already modelled in `DispatchSpawnSummary`)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Must change:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 `sam_status` handler (lines 228\u2013250)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py` \u2014 `get_plan_status()` (lines 422\u2013461)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 `PlanStatus` model (lines 492\u2013504)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 new `dispatch_milestone_status` tool or `dispatch_wave_status` extension (lines 3803\u20133870)\\n\\n**Reference:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` \u2014 `DispatchSpawnSummary` (lines 1403\u20131414), `DispatchWaveSummary` (lines 1385\u20131400)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `sam_status` callers: any orchestrator monitoring plan health (`skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md`, `skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md`, dispatch workflows)\\n- `dispatch_wave_status` callers: kage-bunshin health monitoring (`skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/health.py`)\\n- No callers broken \u2014 all new fields are additive; existing fields unchanged\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**P2** \u2014 orchestrators cannot distinguish a progressing plan from a deadlocked one without inspecting every task individually. `dispatch_wave_status` requires O(N waves) calls to get a milestone view.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Orchestrators can self-correct (re-dispatch or escalate stuck tasks) without human polling\\n- Single-call milestone aggregate for `dispatch_wave_status` reduces O(N waves) to 1 call\\n- `stuck_tasks` list enables targeted alerting rather than full task inspection\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**`sam_status` extensions:**\\n- [ ] Returns `stuck_tasks: list[{task_id, in_progress_seconds}]` for every in-progress task where `started` is set and `(now - started) > stuck_threshold`\\n- [ ] Accepts optional `stuck_threshold_minutes: int = 120` parameter\\n- [ ] Returns `avg_cycle_time_seconds: float | None` \u2014 mean of `(completed - started).total_seconds()` across complete tasks with both timestamps; `null` when fewer than one complete task qualifies\\n- [ ] Returns `throughput_per_hour: float | None` \u2014 `complete_count / elapsed_hours` from earliest `started` to `now`; `null` when no started task exists\\n- [ ] All new fields are `null` (not zero) when insufficient data \u2014 prevents silent false-zero reporting\\n- [ ] Existing callers without `stuck_threshold_minutes` see unchanged behavior for existing fields\\n\\n**Milestone aggregate:**\\n- [ ] New `dispatch_milestone_status(milestone)` tool OR `wave_num=None` sentinel on `dispatch_wave_status` returns cross-wave aggregate matching `DispatchSpawnSummary` shape: `waves_executed`, `total_items`, `completed`, `failed`, `skipped`, `elapsed_seconds`, `per_wave`, `total_cost`\\n\\n**Tests:**\\n- [ ] Unit tests cover: zero in-progress tasks, one stuck task, one fast task, mixed states\\n- [ ] `avg_cycle_time_seconds` with no complete tasks returns `null`\\n- [ ] Milestone aggregate with two waves returns correct sums\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**STANDARD** \u2014 ~2\u20133 hours implementation + tests. Two coordinated changes: (1) `PlanStatus` model extension + metric computation in `get_plan_status` (timestamp arithmetic, all data available); (2) new milestone-aggregate endpoint (counter summation, model already exists).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using SAM for multi-agent plan orchestration**, I want **`sam_status` to include stuck-task detection and cycle-time metrics, and a milestone-aggregate endpoint for `dispatch_wave_status`** so that **orchestrators can self-correct without human polling**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research finding \u2014 mcp-ux-improvements-20260404.md, validated mcp-ux-improvements-validation-20260404.md\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Groomed**: 2026-04-09\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current Behavior Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**`sam_status`:** calls `get_plan_status()` (`sam_schema/core/query.py:422\u2013461`) which returns `PlanStatus` with exactly 7 fields: `feature`, `total_tasks`, `by_status`, `ready_tasks`, `blocked_tasks`, `completion_pct`, `has_cycles`. No timestamps. The `Task` model (`sam_schema/core/models.py:107\u2013248`) holds `created`, `started`, `completed`, and `last_activity` datetime fields \u2014 none surfaced by `get_plan_status`.\\n\\n**`dispatch_wave_status`:** (`backlog_core/server.py:3803\u20133870`) scoped to a single `(milestone, wave_num)` pair \u2014 no milestone-aggregate endpoint. `DispatchSpawnSummary` (`backlog_core/models.py:1403\u20131414`) already models the aggregate shape (`waves_executed`, `total_items`, `completed`, `failed`, `elapsed_seconds`, `per_wave`, `total_cost`) but is only produced as the final result of `dispatch_spawn`, not queryable mid-run.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current Behavior (Evidence)\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**`sam_status`:** calls `get_plan_status()` (`sam_schema/core/query.py:422\u2013461`) which returns `PlanStatus` with exactly 7 fields: `feature`, `total_tasks`, `by_status`, `ready_tasks`, `blocked_tasks`, `completion_pct`, `has_cycles`. No timestamps. The `Task` model (`sam_schema/core/models.py:107\u2013248`) holds `created`, `started`, `completed`, and `last_activity` datetime fields \u2014 none surfaced by `get_plan_status`.\\n\\n**`dispatch_wave_status`:** (`backlog_core/server.py:3803\u20133870`) scoped to a single `(milestone, wave_num)` pair \u2014 no milestone-aggregate endpoint. `DispatchSpawnSummary` (`backlog_core/models.py:1403\u20131414`) already models the aggregate shape (`waves_executed`, `total_items`, `completed`, `failed`, `elapsed_seconds`, `per_wave`, `total_cost`) but is only produced as the final result of `dispatch_spawn`, not queryable mid-run.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**`sam_status` \u2014 extend `get_plan_status()`:**\\n\\n```python\\n# Add to PlanStatus model:\\nstuck_tasks: list[dict] = []\\navg_cycle_time_seconds: float | None = None\\nthroughput_per_hour: float | None = None\\n\\n# Add to get_plan_status() signature:\\ndef get_plan_status(plan_path, stuck_threshold_minutes: int = 120) -> PlanStatus:\\n    now = datetime.now(tz=UTC)\\n    threshold = timedelta(minutes=stuck_threshold_minutes)\\n    cycle_times, stuck = [], []\\n    earliest_started = None\\n    for task in tasks:\\n        if task.started:\\n            if earliest_started is None or task.started < earliest_started:\\n                earliest_started = task.started\\n        if task.status == \\\"in-progress\\\" and task.started:\\n            secs = (now - task.started).total_seconds()\\n            if timedelta(seconds=secs) > threshold:\\n                stuck.append({\\\"task_id\\\": task.id, \\\"in_progress_seconds\\\": int(secs)})\\n        if task.status == \\\"complete\\\" and task.started and task.completed:\\n            cycle_times.append((task.completed - task.started).total_seconds())\\n    # compute metrics\\n```\\n\\n**Milestone aggregate \u2014 preferred option A:**\\n\\nNew `dispatch_milestone_status(milestone: str)` tool that calls `mgr.get_all_waves(milestone)`, sums `DispatchWaveSummary` fields, returns `DispatchSpawnSummary`-shaped dict. Verify `DispatchStateManager` exposes wave iteration before choosing option; add method if not.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"34e727474f967e9b4cfeb329af6a0dd05f9bd36e96dbda77c333c29948858999\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdrgSA\"}"}